      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "optical",
        "summary": "In CH3CN, 1 shows typical Yb(III) NIR emission at 983 nm (2F5/2→2F7/2) with ligand-centered excitation at 298 and 378 nm (antenna/LMET). Lifetime 8.05 μs, emission quantum yield 0.06(±0.01)%, intrinsic Yb quantum yield 0.40%, estimated LMET efficiency ~15%. NIR luminescence is quenched by anions and nitro explosives, most strongly by F− and picric acid (PA), with KSV 4.01×10^4 M−1 and 8.57×10^4 M−1 and LODs 6.72×10−7 M and 3.14×10−7 M, respectively; quenching of F− and PA is not disrupted by other anions or explosives.",
